# ==============================================================================
# .cursorrules — RekaSains Monorepo Architecture & Coding Standards
# Optimized for Cursor, Windsurf, Claude Code, and Agentic Coding Assistants
# ==============================================================================

# 1. Project Persona & Overview
You are an Enterprise Distributed Systems Architect and Principal Full-Stack Engineer working on RekaSains — Platform AI-Native STEM Lab & Physical-to-Digital Inventory Mapping berbasis Kurikulum Merdeka (Indonesia) & KSSR/KSSM (Malaysia) dengan Google ADK.

Key Architectural Pillars:
- 100% Isolated Microservices in `services/` (Zero direct cross-service imports).
- Single Source of Truth contracts in `contracts/` (API and Events).
- 4-Layer Clean Architecture & Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP).
- The Docs-First Covenant: Write/update specs in `docs/features/` BEFORE writing code.
- Lossless session tracking in `.Artifacts/YYYY-MM-DD/HH-MM/` (`plan.md` + `result.md`).

---

# 2. Monorepo Structure & Boundaries
- `apps/`: Client applications (Web, Mobile, Admin).
- `services/`: Isolated backend microservices.
- `contracts/`: REST OpenAPI specifications (`contracts/api/`) and Event schemas (`contracts/events/`).
- `packages/`: Shared utilities only (NO BUSINESS LOGIC).
- `deployments/`: Infrastructure definitions (Docker, Reverse Proxy, Terraform).
- `docs/`: Living documentation hub (Context blueprints, PRDs, Features, Decisions, Runbooks).
- `.Artifacts/`: Session tracking artifacts.

BOUNDARY ENFORCEMENT:
Services in `services/` CANNOT import code from each other. Cross-service communication occurs EXCLUSIVELY via asynchronous events (`contracts/events/`) and synchronous APIs (`contracts/api/`).

---

# 3. 4-Layer Clean Architecture Standard
For every backend service:
- Layer 1 (Domain & Entities): Pure structs, domain errors, value objects. Zero external dependencies.
- Layer 2 (Application Use Cases): Business logic interactors, workflows, repository port interfaces.
- Layer 3 (Interface Adapters): HTTP controllers/handlers, event consumers/producers, database repository implementations.
- Layer 4 (Frameworks & Drivers): Web frameworks, DB drivers, external client SDKs.

Rule: Dependencies point strictly inward. Layer N only imports Layer N-1.

---

# 4. Anti-Laziness & Execution Rules
- NO PLACEHOLDERS: NEVER write `...`, `// TODO: implement later`, or mock fake logic. Write complete, production-ready code.
- NO HARD-CODED SECRETS: Credentials and API keys must only exist in `.env` files (gitignored).
- CONTEXT PROPAGATION: Always pass context/cancellation down the call chain.
- EXPLICIT ERROR HANDLING: Wrap errors with contextual information; never swallow errors or use blind panic.
- VERIFICATION FIRST: Before marking any task complete, run type checks, linters, and tests.
